WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:04.462
Welcome to the final episode
of this season's Wine Down.

00:00:04.546 --> 00:00:07.424
Today we are joined by
the incredible Amanda Seales,

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:08.591
who plays Tiffany.

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:12.721
She'll be helping us break down
tonight's episode,
"Lowkey Lost".

00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:14.431
♪ (UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:18.184
A huge part of the episode is

00:00:18.268 --> 00:00:20.562
dealing with really
needing to find Tiffany.

00:00:20.645 --> 00:00:22.564
Why do you guys feel
it was important for us

00:00:22.647 --> 00:00:25.859
to sort of tackle Tiffany's
story line evolving around

00:00:25.942 --> 00:00:27.360
post-partum depression?

00:00:27.777 --> 00:00:29.696
We wanted to depict this
because, you know,

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:33.032
it's commonplace, and we wanted
to show this struggle.

00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:35.952
And just felt like
this was the natural opportunity

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:37.162
to showcase this.

00:00:37.245 --> 00:00:40.165
Tiffany's the only mother,
the only married one

00:00:40.248 --> 00:00:43.543
out of our group of friends,
and she already started to feel

00:00:43.626 --> 00:00:45.170
isolated in a way,
and so

00:00:45.253 --> 00:00:47.922
unfortunately this just added
to her burden.

00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:51.551
I think Tiff had also
kind of like, solidified herself

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:54.179
as the strong one.
Like, even though she'll allude

00:00:54.262 --> 00:00:56.014
to, like, things with Derek.
It's never, like,

00:00:56.097 --> 00:00:57.307
been put in her girls' laps.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:01.019
And, so, I think that also
just reflects the reality of,

00:01:01.102 --> 00:01:04.314
"You know, I had a strong mind
but not necessarily
a healthy mind."

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.524
So we know how to muscle through
and like,

00:01:06.608 --> 00:01:08.860
"That's not gon' break me,
and that's not gon' hurt me."

00:01:08.943 --> 00:01:12.238
But it's like are you really
dealing with it?

00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:14.783
Or are you just
suppressing sadness?

00:01:14.866 --> 00:01:16.242
But that's that character,
right?

00:01:16.326 --> 00:01:18.244
AMANDA:
She set this grid up.

00:01:18.328 --> 00:01:20.872
Like, my hair is gon' be
together, my--

00:01:20.955 --> 00:01:22.582
I even made, like,
a conscious decision

00:01:22.665 --> 00:01:25.168
over the course of the season
to, like, let my nails be

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:28.254
less done, so that by the end

00:01:28.338 --> 00:01:29.756
she doesn't even
have a manicure,

00:01:29.839 --> 00:01:33.760
which for Tiffany, that's like--
You've never seen Tiffany

00:01:33.843 --> 00:01:35.512
without this happening.

00:01:36.012 --> 00:01:37.931
But, like, I think a lot
of women can relate to

00:01:38.014 --> 00:01:40.391
something that might not be
very indicative of, like,

00:01:40.475 --> 00:01:41.851
them falling apart.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.813
Because a lot of times it'll be
those little things that

00:01:44.896 --> 00:01:46.689
you just know are, like,
"Oh, she's together."

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.274
And I think that was
another factor, too,

00:01:48.358 --> 00:01:50.151
because, yes, Tiffany's
going through this thing,

00:01:50.235 --> 00:01:52.362
but we also wanted it to serve
as a metaphor for

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.239
her actual friends
missing out.

00:01:54.322 --> 00:01:57.116
Like, her actual friends
aren't noticing that

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.953
she's falling apart,
and that is also indicative

00:02:00.036 --> 00:02:01.621
of the friendship that
they have with each other.

00:02:01.704 --> 00:02:03.122
They're not seeing one another.

00:02:03.206 --> 00:02:04.624
You know who was in it, though?

00:02:04.707 --> 00:02:05.708
BOTH: Derek.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.502
Derek was in it. (LAUGHS)

00:02:07.585 --> 00:02:10.547
Derek was down.
That's what's great,

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:13.091
I think, at the door,
when you guys have

00:02:13.174 --> 00:02:15.969
that moment together where
you'd never let Derek see

00:02:16.052 --> 00:02:17.262
the other side of that, right?

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.306
And I think even not wanting
to answer the door, right?

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:23.643
"How do I face this man who
I typically am together for?

00:02:23.726 --> 00:02:25.478
I don't want him to really see
me like this,

00:02:25.562 --> 00:02:26.646
'cause what does that mean?

00:02:26.729 --> 00:02:28.314
How will he see me now
going forward?"

00:02:28.398 --> 00:02:29.983
It still gives me chills
thinking about it

00:02:30.066 --> 00:02:31.025
because it was so real,

00:02:31.359 --> 00:02:33.611
about a husband and wife
who do need to see each other.

00:02:33.695 --> 00:02:34.612
It's scary.

00:02:34.696 --> 00:02:35.989
You know why else
it give you chills?

00:02:36.072 --> 00:02:37.907
-PRENTICE: Why's that?
-Because I was actin', baby!

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:40.910
(LAUGHTER)

00:02:43.746 --> 00:02:45.790
One of the things we discussed
in the room, was from

00:02:45.874 --> 00:02:48.626
a very early stand point,
was wanting to tackle

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:51.087
this topic of Tiffany
this year, so...

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:53.339
I would love to talk about how
post-partum depression

00:02:53.423 --> 00:02:56.426
is rarely really portrayed
accurately on TV.

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:57.969
Especially with black women.

00:02:58.052 --> 00:03:00.430
When it is portrayed it's...
(LAUGHS)

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:01.723
It's wild.

00:03:01.973 --> 00:03:03.558
ALL: (LAUGH)

00:03:03.641 --> 00:03:05.810
"I can't take this baby."

00:03:05.894 --> 00:03:08.187
You know, it's being acted to
the back of the room.

00:03:08.605 --> 00:03:10.273
Not to the cameras.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:13.026
It's not nuanced. We talk about
that a lot in the room.

00:03:13.109 --> 00:03:15.445
I remember to a point that
we were talking about

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.739
debating what's the most real
version of

00:03:17.822 --> 00:03:19.574
what she would be wearing,
how you would find her,

00:03:19.657 --> 00:03:21.492
what she would do,
has she eaten?

00:03:21.576 --> 00:03:23.494
We got very meticulous
about this,

00:03:23.578 --> 00:03:25.663
because we wanted it to feel
very real.

00:03:25.747 --> 00:03:27.332
Yeah!
You talked about your nails.

00:03:27.415 --> 00:03:31.294
What else did you do to prepare
for Tiffany's post-partum?

00:03:31.628 --> 00:03:34.088
I think the hardest thing
was gonna be

00:03:34.172 --> 00:03:37.091
just figuring out an authentic
place to tap into that could

00:03:37.175 --> 00:03:40.136
get me to the same feeling
of emptiness and confusion

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:42.221
that you would be at
if this was,

00:03:42.305 --> 00:03:43.723
you know, your actual reality.

00:03:44.265 --> 00:03:45.600
Speaking of pregnancies...

00:03:46.351 --> 00:03:49.979
There's a big drop at the end
of this episode,

00:03:50.188 --> 00:03:53.232
of Lawrence getting Condola
pregnant.

00:03:53.316 --> 00:03:55.693
How do you think Issa feels
about that

00:03:55.777 --> 00:03:57.654
and she and Lawrence's
relationship,

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:58.780
possibly, moving forward?

00:03:58.863 --> 00:04:01.115
This taints him in
a very real way.

00:04:01.199 --> 00:04:02.659
-And I say that--
-Does it?

00:04:03.159 --> 00:04:06.287
To me, if I'm interested in
a man and he has a child

00:04:06.371 --> 00:04:09.832
with someone else,
I think it robs you of

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:12.168
that moment. And that's my mind.

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:13.753
I feel like they've lost
a milestone.

00:04:13.836 --> 00:04:16.756
In the season two finale,
like, when she pictured

00:04:16.839 --> 00:04:18.841
getting back with Lawrence,
having a baby together

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.218
is the first thing.
So, now--

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:21.552
She don't got the first born.

00:04:21.636 --> 00:04:22.804
She doesn't have
the first born.

00:04:22.887 --> 00:04:24.555
He's sharing that moment
with someone else.

00:04:24.639 --> 00:04:28.101
Someone who he's not with,
and they've just recommitted.

00:04:28.518 --> 00:04:30.103
So, there's things to discuss,

00:04:30.186 --> 00:04:32.981
like how active he wants to be
in his child's life.

00:04:33.064 --> 00:04:35.817
If he's not active,
then he's kind of not shit.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:37.652
(OVERLAPPING CHATTER)

00:04:37.735 --> 00:04:39.404
So, you're like
an antsy girlfriend?

00:04:39.737 --> 00:04:42.323
If-- Can Issa and Condola
be friends?

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:45.868
-You were already friends.
-Not after that.

00:04:46.244 --> 00:04:47.453
It's gon' be lit.

00:04:47.537 --> 00:04:49.664
(LAUGHTER)

00:04:51.499 --> 00:04:54.794
Thank you so much for joining us
for Wine Down this season.

00:04:54.877 --> 00:04:56.879
We really hope you enjoyed
watching this season

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:59.632
as much as we loved making it.
Cheers.

00:04:59.716 --> 00:05:03.928
-Cheers! It's over y'all.
-Cheers to the season cuatro!

